#Eepo-prep.lic
#Rogue version of Brayis-prep.lic (Eepo) -- as basic as possible: no spells, no rubs
#(no rub items), and nothing that stores or swaps his two longswords, since his STORE
#and READY settings were never captured and his profiles never needed a ready command
#(he rests with the swords in hand). All this does is check he is armed, then start the
#shared helpers.

module EepoPrep

# eloot's sell does STORE WEAPON then READY WEAPON, so after a rest the swords should be
# back in hand. Right hand empty -> try READY WEAPON once.
fput "ready weapon" if checkright.nil?

# Still nothing in the right hand: the weapon is really gone (disarmed and never
# recovered, or the READY weapon setting points at something that isn't there). Don't let
# bigshot walk back out unarmed -- stop it here, in town, the same way Brayis-prep.lic does.
pause 0.5
if checkright.nil?
  echo "Eepo-prep: nothing in the right hand -- stopping bigshot. " \
       "Check the READY / STORE weapon settings (READY LIST, STORE LIST)."
  Script.kill("bigshot") if Script.running?("bigshot")
  exit
end

# Puts away loot eloot has no room for and unpauses it, so a full cloak can't
# leave you fighting with your hands full (see eloot_guard.lic).
Script.start("eloot_guard") unless Script.running?("eloot_guard")

# Rescue-child bounty: when the child finds you mid-hunt, stop and run echild right there
# instead of hunting on with her in tow (two children died that way 11/07; see child_watch.lic;
# ;vars set child_rescue=off to disable).
Script.start("child_watch") unless Script.running?("child_watch")

end #End of module
